                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I almost dismissed this game entirely after playing for 3 minutes, but decided to go back and give it another go. It didn't change my mind, but did let me see the potential the game has a little more.\n\nMy main gripe with the game is the bow - it's without a doubt the worst I've used in all the archery games I've played so far. That's quite a big problem when the games entire premise is based around archery. The models are simplistic and uninspiring. \n\nWhat this game does right however, is introduce some interesting game elements that other archery games lack. For example, not only are you shooting arrows - you are being shot at and will actively have to dodge arrows in a neo-esque manner. That's good fun and energetic. Other enemies put ladders against the side of the keep and you have to run over and push them away. It all mixes it up and a bit, so you don't feel you're stuck in a rut of shooting arrow after arrow waiting for your hands to cramp up.\n\nIn its current state, I don't consider this game mature enough to recommend it, but I will keep an eye on future developments. If you're looking for an archery game - this would be far from the top of my list. The Lab (free), God of Arrows and Quivr are all far better. If I had to pick one, I'd pick Quivr as the multiplayer experience is great and the developer is very active and listens to its users.",
